  <a class="back" href="/">← the hall</a>
  <h1>The saga, <em>at home</em></h1>
  <p>Ymir is one substrate, one machine, all realms carved from it — and every
  Norse name is load-bearing: it explains the machine's job. The hall keeps the
  lore itself; no cloud door carries it.</p>
  <h2>the map</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>name</th><th>what it is</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Ymir</td><td>the substrate — one repo, one machine, all realms from it</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Brokk</td><td>the counsellor — plans, steers, reviews, sends the workers out</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Eindri</td><td>the doers — isolated smiths in the sandboxes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Kaia</td><td>the eye that remembers — the orchestrator</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Yggdrasil</td><td>the world-tree — worktree isolation, zero collision</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Utgard</td><td>the ephemeral sandbox — untrusted code never enters the halls</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mimirsbrunn</td><td>the memory well — long-term memory, embeddings</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Ratatoskr</td><td>the A2A spine — agent-to-agent talk</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Hlidskjalf</td><td>the high seat — the control plane</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Óðrerir</td><td>the mead — this hall, the planning glass</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Bifrost/Heimdall</td><td>the bridge and its guard — every crossing passes over it</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Gjallarhorn</td><td>the horn — the outbound encrypted tunnel</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Runes</td><td>the append-only ledger — every action carved, never un-carved</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Mjollnir</td><td>the hammer — issue to PR, strikes and returns</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Gungnir</td><td>the spear — skill synthesis, forged and validated</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Nornir</td><td>the fates — the schedule, the daily briefing</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Sága</td><td>the seeress — the session start digest</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Muninn/Huginn</td><td>the ravens — memory's curation and the daily observation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Skuld</td><td>the hall's book — the tickets and the plans, the debts owed</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Bölþorn</td><td>the runes' porch — the skills well, taught on demand</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Gróta</td><td>the updater — renews and mends forward</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Eir</td><td>the healer — diagnoses every surface, mends what is broken</td></tr>
  </table>
  <h2>the law, in one breath</h2>
  <p>One hall, many forges. A seat loads its own figure and never takes the
  helm. The boards are shown, not written from the glass — the write door lives
  in the hall's own machinery, and the book keeps what is owed.</p>
</main>
